Error: Jet.UnusedLocalBinding: Local binding `name` is never read.
  --> Tests/UILint/lambda_binding_body_is_never_read.jet:6:9
    |
  5 |     names: [1, 2].map(fn(n) { name: n })
    |                               ^^^^
 Why: A binding that no later expression reads adds dead code and may hide a computed result that should have been used.
 Fix: To give back a record, write `{ {name: value} }`; otherwise remove the binding, or rename `name` to `_name` when the value must be computed.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.UnusedLocalBinding
